# Sport package conventions

- Keep declarative data in JSON validated by `schemas/v0`. Do not put business logic in schemas.
- Required layout: manifest, variants, rules, roster, field, formations, animations, scoreboards, assets/manifest, locales, docs, fixtures, tests.
- Variants must cite `official_source` (title, https URL, retrieved_on, optional version_label), jurisdiction, and effective_date.
- Fiction fixtures and schema smokes set `"fiction": true`. Never invent real teams, players, or rule text.
- Exceptional executable modules require an entry in `exceptional-modules.allowlist.json` and in `manifest.exceptional_modules`. No remote eval (`eval`, `Function`, URL imports, `vm.run*`).
- Run `npm run check`, `npm run validate`, and `npm test` before claiming a package ready.
